---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe41.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — a Single Standard Consolidating Prior Scattered Disclosures" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Significant Judgements in Determining Control, Joint Control, or Significant Influence" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Disclosures About Subsidiaries" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Disclosures About Joint Arrangements and Associates" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Unconsolidated Structured Entities" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Non-Controlling Interests That Are Material to the Group" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Disclosing a Material Non-Controlling Interest" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Disclosing an Unconsolidated Structured Entity's Maximum Exposure to Loss" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 12" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A single, comprehensive disclosure standard spanning all types of interests</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 41 CONSOLIDATES disclosure REQUIREMENTS for an ENTERPRISE'S interests in SUBSIDIARIES, JOINT arrangements, ASSOCIATES, and UNCONSOLIDATED structured ENTITIES — HELPING users EVALUATE the NATURE of, and RISKS associated WITH, these INTERESTS, and THEIR effects on the ENTERPRISE'S financial POSITION and PERFORMANCE. THIS Standard is CLOSELY converged with IFRS 12 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — a Single Standard Consolidating Prior Scattered Disclosures</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Bringing together previously dispersed disclosure requirements</div><div class="principle">BEFORE this Standard, disclosure REQUIREMENTS relating to SUBSIDIARIES, JOINT arrangements, and ASSOCIATES were SCATTERED across THEIR respective INDIVIDUAL standards (ASBE No. 33, No. 40, and No. 2). ASBE No. 41 CONSOLIDATES these DISCLOSURE requirements into ONE unified STANDARD — PARALLELING how IFRS 12 CONSOLIDATED the EQUIVALENT disclosure REQUIREMENTS internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Significant Judgements in Determining Control, Joint Control, or Significant Influence</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Explaining the basis for classification, especially in ambiguous cases</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise DISCLOSES the SIGNIFICANT judgements and ASSUMPTIONS made in DETERMINING WHETHER it HAS control, JOINT control, or SIGNIFICANT influence OVER another entity — PARTICULARLY where the DETERMINATION is NOT straightforward (e.g. DE FACTO control WITHOUT a majority VOTING interest — see the COMPANION ASBE No. 33 poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Disclosures About Subsidiaries</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Composition of the group and non-controlling interests</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise DISCLOSES the COMPOSITION of the GROUP, the INTERESTS non-CONTROLLING shareholders HOLD in the GROUP'S activities and CASH flows, and (WHERE material) SUMMARISED financial INFORMATION about EACH subsidiary WITH material NON-CONTROLLING interests.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Disclosures About Joint Arrangements and Associates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Nature, extent, and financial effects</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise DISCLOSES the NATURE, extent, and FINANCIAL effects of ITS interests in JOINT arrangements and ASSOCIATES — INCLUDING summarised FINANCIAL information for EACH material JOINT venture or ASSOCIATE, and the NATURE of RISKS associated WITH these interests.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Unconsolidated Structured Entities</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Disclosure even where consolidation is not required</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise DISCLOSES information ABOUT its INVOLVEMENT with STRUCTURED entities it does NOT CONSOLIDATE — INCLUDING the NATURE and EXTENT of its INTERESTS, and its MAXIMUM exposure to LOSS FROM those interests — HELPING readers UNDERSTAND risks that MIGHT not otherwise be APPARENT from the CONSOLIDATED financial statements ALONE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Non-Controlling Interests That Are Material to the Group</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Extra transparency where minority shareholders hold a meaningful stake</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a SUBSIDIARY has NON-CONTROLLING interests that are MATERIAL to the GROUP, ADDITIONAL summarised FINANCIAL information is DISCLOSED for THAT subsidiary SPECIFICALLY — ENSURING readers UNDERSTAND the SCALE and NATURE of the MINORITY shareholders' STAKE in the GROUP'S overall PERFORMANCE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Disclosing a Material Non-Controlling Interest</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Summarised financial information for a specific subsidiary</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 60%-owned subsidiary representing a significant portion of group profit</div><div class="wk-body">A group's 60%-owned subsidiary contributes a material portion of consolidated net profit, with the remaining 40% held by non-controlling shareholders.</div><div class="wk-answer">The GROUP discloses SUMMARISED financial INFORMATION SPECIFICALLY for THIS subsidiary — REVENUE, profit, TOTAL assets, TOTAL liabilities, and DIVIDENDS paid to NON-CONTROLLING interests — GIVEN the MATERIALITY of the MINORITY stake to the GROUP'S overall results.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Disclosing an Unconsolidated Structured Entity's Maximum Exposure to Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Quantifying risk from an entity outside the consolidated group</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A sponsored securitisation vehicle</div><div class="wk-body">A company sponsors (but does not consolidate) a securitisation vehicle, retaining a subordinated interest of RMB 15,000,000 and providing a guarantee capped at RMB 5,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company DISCLOSES its MAXIMUM exposure to LOSS from this UNCONSOLIDATED structured ENTITY as RMB 15,000,000 + RMB 5,000,000 = <strong>RMB 20,000,000</strong>, GIVING readers a CLEAR picture of the RISK involved, DESPITE the entity FALLING outside the CONSOLIDATED group.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 41 requires (summary)</div><div class="check-list"><span>Significant judgements in determining control, joint control, or significant influence</span><span>Summarised financial information for material subsidiaries with non-controlling interests, joint ventures, and associates</span><span>Nature and extent of, and maximum exposure to loss from, unconsolidated structured entities</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Which non-controlling interests, joint ventures, and associates are material enough to warrant separate summarised disclosure</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Maximum exposure to loss from unconsolidated structured entities</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 12</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 41 vs IFRS 12</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 41</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 12</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Consolidated disclosure standard</span><span>YES — spans subsidiaries, joint arrangements, associates, structured entities</span><span>YES — same scope, converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — BOTH ASBE and IFRS TOOK the SAME structural APPROACH of CONSOLIDATING previously SCATTERED disclosure REQUIREMENTS into ONE unified STANDARD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every disclosed interest lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>All disclosures under this Standard</span><span>Notes only</span><span>No effect on primary financial statement figures</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 33</span><span>Consolidated Financial Statements — supplies the control determination this Standard's disclosures explain</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 40</span><span>Joint Venture Arrangements — supplies the joint control classification this Standard's disclosures explain</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Structured entity</div><div class="glossary-def">An entity designed so that voting or similar rights are not the dominant factor in deciding who controls it, often relying instead on contractual arrangements.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Maximum exposure to loss</div><div class="glossary-def">The total potential loss an entity could incur from its involvement with an unconsolidated structured entity, disclosed to convey risk beyond the consolidated Balance Sheet.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe41 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
